WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:03.257
Everyone tracks Day 1 Day 7 and Day 30

2
00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.118
retention but almost nobody uses those numbers

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.810
to see what happens next Start by entering

4
00:00:08.822 --> 00:00:11.695
your cohort size how many users you are measuring

5
00:00:12.091 --> 00:00:14.712
Add your Day 1 retention the share still active

6
00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:17.620
a day later Then Day 7 Then Day 30

7
00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:20.216
The calculator fits a decay curve through your

8
00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:23.065
Day 1 and Day 30 figures then checks it

9
00:00:23.077 --> 00:00:25.709
against the Day 7 you entered a close match

10
00:00:25.721 --> 00:00:28.389
means your curve is smooth a big gap flags

11
00:00:28.401 --> 00:00:30.457
something worth investigating From there it

12
00:00:30.469 --> 00:00:34.483
projects forward Day 90 Day 180 a full year

13
00:00:34.844 --> 00:00:36.707
so you can see roughly how many of today's

14
00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:39.375
users are still around long term Every number

15
00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:41.983
updates instantly it runs entirely in your

16
00:00:41.995 --> 00:00:44.748
browser and nothing you type is ever uploaded

17
00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.385
or stored
